{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Infix","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeStepBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeStepBound","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L157-L164","doc":"**`C(A,2) − (A−1) = C(A−1,2)`** — the appendix's Hecke-step budget: one reduction per crossing\nafter the first at each generator. Stated *after* the computations above and proved via Pascal, so\nthe arithmetic reads as bookkeeping rather than as the content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.no_yangBaxter_pattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.no_yangBaxter_pattern","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L146-L153","doc":"**No Yang–Baxter pattern.**  Its leading word is `σⱼσᵢσⱼ`, which repeats the letter `σⱼ`; a\nstrictly increasing word is injective along adjacencies, so `j < i < j` is impossible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.no_farComm_pattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.no_farComm_pattern","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L137-L144","doc":"**No far-commutativity pattern.**  Its leading word is `σⱼσᵢ` with `j ≥ i + 2`; adjacent letters\nin a strictly increasing word satisfy `j < i` instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.no_hecke_pattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.no_hecke_pattern","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L129-L135","doc":"**No Hecke pattern.**  A strictly increasing index word has no repeated adjacent letter, so no\nsubword `σᵢσᵢ` — the leading word of the Hecke rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.transferMatrix_scalar_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.transferMatrix_scalar_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L115-L121","doc":"**A purely scalar crossing costs nothing.**  At `c = 0` the transfer matrix is `d • 1`, so the\nchain coefficients merely rescale and no `σ²` is ever created — the case the appendix flags\nparenthetically when it says no Hecke step is spent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeStep_eq_transferMatrix_snd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeStep_eq_transferMatrix_snd","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L109-L113","doc":"The second component of the same identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeStep_eq_transferMatrix_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeStep_eq_transferMatrix_fst","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L102-L107","doc":"**The block step is the transfer matrix.**  The coefficient pair produced by one Hecke\nreduction is exactly `T(c,d) ⬝ᵥ (a,b)` — first component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.transferMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.transferMatrix","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L98-L100","doc":"The transfer matrix `T(c,d)` of the appendix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeRelation_satisfiable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeRelation_satisfiable","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L93-L96","doc":"**The Hecke hypothesis is satisfiable** — a guard against a vacuously-true conditional.\n`σ = 1`, `qq = 0` over `ℤ` satisfies `σ² = qq·σ + 1`, so `hecke_linear_mul` is not quantified over\nan empty set of instances. (A faithful `H_A(q)` instance is out of scope — see the header.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.hecke_linear_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.hecke_linear_mul","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L82-L91","doc":"**The block step.**  In any commutative ring containing `σ` with `σ² = qq·σ + 1`, the product of\ntwo linear forms in `σ` is again linear, with the stated coefficients.\n\nThis is the inductive step of the appendix's proof. It is *derived from* the Hecke relation, not\nasserted alongside it: the `linear_combination` certificate is `(a*c) * hσ`, so the relation is\ngenuinely load-bearing and a perturbed relation gives a different — false — statement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:tm-gs-normal-form","label":"prop:tm-gs-normal-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-transfer-matrices/tm-gs-normal-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TransferMatrices.GSNormalForm.heckeScalar","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/TransferMatrices/GSNormalForm.lean#L77-L78","doc":"The Hecke scalar `q − q⁻¹`, built from a unit so no field structure is required. ","signatureChunk":0}]}